# .sanitization-allowlist
#
# One glob or path per line (matched against the path exactly as returned
# by `git ls-files`, i.e. repo-root-relative). Lines starting with '#' and
# blank lines are ignored. Files/paths matching an entry here are exempt
# from the "sanitization" workflow's internal-disclosure scan (Check 2:
# the internal homelab domain subdomains, 192.168.1.x homelab subnet addresses).
#
# Default posture is fail-closed: a file NOT listed here that contains a
# real internal identifier will fail CI. Only add an entry if the match is
# a legitimate false positive (e.g. doctrine text explaining what NOT to
# leak) -- never to launder an actual leak to green.
#
# No entries yet.
